  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Envelope 3: Protection, cash and non-food item support for people on the move in north-west Syrian Arab Republic</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This project targets people on the move&#x2014;those preparing to relocate, in transit, or newly arrived in a community. Its core aim is to connect and enhance existing services across Protection and other relevant sectors, improving responsiveness to the unique needs of mobile populations. The approach includes capacity building, provision of specialized tools, and tailored protection services, fostering integration and specialization around emerging risks linked to displacement and mobility. Activities will be delivered through both community centers and mobile teams, maximizing geographic coverage. Protection monitoring will be ongoing, in collaboration with the Protection Monitoring Working Group, to identify new concerns and adapt responses. IOM will utilize its network of 82 active Protection Community Centers as entry points for information sharing, referrals, and service delivery. Based on referrals, IOM will also provide Multi-Purpose Cash Assistance (MPCA) to 2,000 vulnerable households, with each receiving one round of emergency cash (USD 150), aligned with CWG recommendations and SMEB estimates. Additionally, 1,525 households will receive essential Non-Food Items (NFIs) via pre-positioning and rapid response. MPCA and NFI beneficiaries will be distinct, ensuring no overlap in assistance.</narrative>
  </description>
